  "body": "Bumps the website-dependencies group with 8 updates in the / directory:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [@astrojs/mdx](https://github.com/withastro/astro/tree/HEAD/packages/integrations/mdx) | `7.0.3` | `7.0.5` |\n| [@astrojs/netlify](https://github.com/withastro/astro/tree/HEAD/packages/integrations/netlify) | `8.1.2` | `8.2.0` |\n| [@fontsource-variable/ibm-plex-sans](https://github.com/fontsource/font-files/tree/HEAD/fonts/variable/ibm-plex-sans) | `5.2.8` | `5.3.0` |\n| [@fontsource-variable/lora](https://github.com/fontsource/font-files/tree/HEAD/fonts/variable/lora) | `5.2.8` | `5.3.0` |\n| [@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono](https://github.com/fontsource/font-files/tree/HEAD/fonts/google/ibm-plex-mono) | `5.2.7` | `5.3.0` |\n| [astro](https://github.com/withastro/astro/tree/HEAD/packages/astro) | `7.1.1` | `7.2.0` |\n| [shiki](https://github.com/shikijs/shiki/tree/HEAD/packages/shiki) | `4.3.1` | `4.4.2` |\n| [web-vitals](https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals) | `5.3.0` | `6.1.0` |\n\n\nUpdates `@astrojs/mdx` from 7.0.3 to 7.0.5\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/releases\">@​astrojs/mdx's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><code>@​astrojs/mdx</code><a href=\"https://github.com/7\"><code>@​7</code></a>.0.5</h2>\n<h3>Patch Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Updated dependencies [<a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/c895b12b99a73f5a9f98d6699452d12c138f8a18\"><code>c895b12</code></a>]:\n<ul>\n<li><code>@​astrojs/internal-helpers</code><a href=\"https://github.com/0\"><code>@​0</code></a>.10.2</li>\n<li><code>@​astrojs/markdown-remark</code><a href=\"https://github.com/7\"><code>@​7</code></a>.2.2</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><code>@​astrojs/mdx</code><a href=\"https://github.com/7\"><code>@​7</code></a>.0.4</h2>\n<h3>Patch Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/withastro/astro/pull/17514\">#17514</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/41a00dd86fc848763fa9dc6e501d6e85188c1306\"><code>41a00dd</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/gtritchie\"><code>@​gtritchie</code></a>! - Fixes a bug where the integration was emitting React-cased attribute names.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/blob/main/packages/integrations/mdx/CHANGELOG.md\">@​astrojs/mdx's changelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>7.0.5</h2>\n<h3>Patch Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Updated dependencies [<a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/c895b12b99a73f5a9f98d6699452d12c138f8a18\"><code>c895b12</code></a>]:\n<ul>\n<li><code>@​astrojs/internal-helpers</code><a href=\"https://github.com/0\"><code>@​0</code></a>.10.2</li>\n<li><code>@​astrojs/markdown-remark</code><a href=\"https://github.com/7\"><code>@​7</code></a>.2.2</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>7.0.4</h2>\n<h3>Patch Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/withastro/astro/pull/17514\">#17514</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/41a00dd86fc848763fa9dc6e501d6e85188c1306\"><code>41a00dd</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/gtritchie\"><code>@​gtritchie</code></a>! - Fixes a bug where the integration was emitting React-cased attribute names.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/b0535ca0a98846b46a3ab16c52c4d6adda7cfa10\"><code>b0535ca</code></a> [ci] release (<a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/tree/HEAD/packages/integrations/mdx/issues/17528\">#17528</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/112d3ea14cf997218239fd8a436707e56a3815fb\"><code>112d3ea</code></a> [ci] release (<a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/tree/HEAD/packages/integrations/mdx/issues/17469\">#17469</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/41a00dd86fc848763fa9dc6e501d6e85188c1306\"><code>41a00dd</code></a> fix(mdx): emit HTML attribute casing on the Sätteri MDX path (<a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/tree/HEAD/packages/integrations/mdx/issues/17514\">#17514</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commits/@astrojs/mdx@7.0.5/packages/integrations/mdx\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@astrojs/netlify` from 8.1.2 to 8.2.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/releases\">@​astrojs/netlify's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><code>@​astrojs/netlify</code><a href=\"https://github.com/8\"><code>@​8</code></a>.2.0</h2>\n<h3>Minor Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/withastro/astro/pull/16871\">#16871</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/90c98ae21ef0444a4088b7081676b0f97915001f\"><code>90c98ae</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/adamchal\"><code>@​adamchal</code></a>! - When <code>session: false</code> is set in <code>astro.config</code>, the adapter no longer auto-wires the Netlify Blobs session driver. Combined with the matching <code>astro</code> change, this lets the session runtime tree-shake out of the function bundle.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Patch Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Updated dependencies []:\n<ul>\n<li><code>@​astrojs/underscore-redirects</code><a href=\"https://github.com/1\"><code>@​1</code></a>.0.3</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><code>@​astrojs/netlify</code><a href=\"https://github.com/8\"><code>@​8</code></a>.1.3</h2>\n<h3>Patch Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Updated dependencies [<a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/c895b12b99a73f5a9f98d6699452d12c138f8a18\"><code>c895b12</code></a>]:\n<ul>\n<li><code>@​astrojs/internal-helpers</code><a href=\"https://github.com/0\"><code>@​0</code></a>.10.2</li>\n<li><code>@​astrojs/underscore-redirects</code><a href=\"https://github.com/1\"><code>@​1</code></a>.0.3</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/blob/main/packages/integrations/netlify/CHANGELOG.md\">@​astrojs/netlify's changelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>8.2.0</h2>\n<h3>Minor Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/withastro/astro/pull/16871\">#16871</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/90c98ae21ef0444a4088b7081676b0f97915001f\"><code>90c98ae</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/adamchal\"><code>@​adamchal</code></a>! - When <code>session: false</code> is set in <code>astro.config</code>, the adapter no longer auto-wires the Netlify Blobs session driver. Combined with the matching <code>astro</code> change, this lets the session runtime tree-shake out of the function bundle.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Patch Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Updated dependencies []:\n<ul>\n<li><code>@​astrojs/underscore-redirects</code><a href=\"https://github.com/1\"><code>@​1</code></a>.0.3</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>8.1.3</h2>\n<h3>Patch Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Updated dependencies [<a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/c895b12b99a73f5a9f98d6699452d12c138f8a18\"><code>c895b12</code></a>]:\n<ul>\n<li><code>@​astrojs/internal-helpers</code><a href=\"https://github.com/0\"><code>@​0</code></a>.10.2</li>\n<li><code>@​astrojs/underscore-redirects</code><a href=\"https://github.com/1\"><code>@​1</code></a>.0.3</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/60e94329f94438c1fc9b513bd9669bf07c89b680\"><code>60e9432</code></a> [ci] release (<a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/tree/HEAD/packages/integrations/netlify/issues/17558\">#17558</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/90c98ae21ef0444a4088b7081676b0f97915001f\"><code>90c98ae</code></a> feat(session): add <code>session: false</code> to opt out of session support (<a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/tree/HEAD/packages/integrations/netlify/issues/16871\">#16871</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/b0535ca0a98846b46a3ab16c52c4d6adda7cfa10\"><code>b0535ca</code></a> [ci] release (<a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/tree/HEAD/packages/integrations/netlify/issues/17528\">#17528</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commits/@astrojs/netlify@8.2.0/packages/integrations/netlify\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@fontsource-variable/ibm-plex-sans` from 5.2.8 to 5.3.0\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/fontsource/font-files/commits/HEAD/fonts/variable/ibm-plex-sans\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@fontsource-variable/lora` from 5.2.8 to 5.3.0\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/fontsource/font-files/commits/HEAD/fonts/variable/lora\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono` from 5.2.7 to 5.3.0\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/fontsource/font-files/commits/HEAD/fonts/google/ibm-plex-mono\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `astro` from 7.1.1 to 7.2.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/releases\">astro's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>astro@7.2.0</h2>\n<h3>Minor Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/withastro/astro/pull/17174\">#17174</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/0224a3a356c1f2956075b77c3667bc67cf027d8c\"><code>0224a3a</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/matthewp\"><code>@​matthewp</code></a>! - Adds the <code>astro preview --background</code> flag to start preview servers as background processes.</p>\n<p>This makes preview servers easier to manage from scripts and AI coding agents because the command returns after the server is ready instead of keeping the terminal attached to the long-running process.</p>\n<pre lang=\"sh\"><code>astro preview --background\n</code></pre>\n<p>When a preview server is running in the background, you can inspect or stop it with new <code>astro preview</code> subcommands:</p>\n<pre lang=\"sh\"><code>astro preview status\nastro preview logs\nastro preview logs --follow\nastro preview stop\n</code></pre>\n<p>If Astro detects that <code>astro preview</code> is being run by an AI coding agent, background mode is enabled automatically. This matches the existing behavior for <code>astro dev</code>, allowing agents to continue working after the preview server starts while still receiving the server URL and process ID.</p>\n<p>To opt out of automatic background mode for preview servers, set <code>ASTRO_PREVIEW_BACKGROUND=0</code> before running <code>astro preview</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/withastro/astro/pull/17532\">#17532</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/7f94895f8c28fc4d6977c9bfb1f90e80a9cfaa08\"><code>7f94895</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/florian-lefebvre\"><code>@​florian-lefebvre</code></a>! - Adds support for paths relative to your project root in <code>logger.entrypoint</code></p>\n<p>Previously, pointing <code>logger.entrypoint</code> at a custom log handler living in your own project required building an absolute <code>URL</code>. You can now write the path directly:</p>\n<pre lang=\"diff\"><code>// astro.config.mjs\nimport { defineConfig } from 'astro/config';\n<p>export default defineConfig({\nlogger: {</p>\n<ul>\n<li>entrypoint: new URL('./src/logger.js', import.meta.url),</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>entrypoint: './src/logger.js',\n},\n});\n</code></pre></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Paths starting with <code>./</code> or <code>../</code> are resolved against your project root. Package specifiers such as <code>@org/astro-logger</code>, absolute paths, and <code>URL</code> entrypoints keep working as before.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/withastro/astro/pull/17084\">#17084</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/961bbe5fdf4a761adb479595dfb94dc2e80f2957\"><code>961bbe5</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/matthewp\"><code>@​matthewp</code></a>! - Widens the <code>AstroPrerenderer</code> <code>render()</code> return type so prerenderers can report incremental-build metadata</p>\n<p>A prerenderer's <code>render()</code> may now resolve to either a <code>Response</code> (as before) or a <code>PrerenderResult</code> object that pairs the response with the content entries and optimized-image transforms the page resolved. This lets prerenderers that render out of process (for example, in an adapter's runtime like workerd) report those dependencies back to the build, so <a href=\"https://docs.astro.build/en/reference/experimental-flags/incremental-build/\">incremental static builds</a> can track and replay them for skipped pages.</p>\n<pre lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { AstroPrerenderer, PrerenderResult } from 'astro';\n<p>const prerenderer: AstroPrerenderer = {\n</code></pre></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/blob/main/packages/astro/CHANGELOG.md\">astro's changelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>7.2.0</h2>\n<h3>Minor Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/withastro/astro/pull/17174\">#17174</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/0224a3a356c1f2956075b77c3667bc67cf027d8c\"><code>0224a3a</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/matthewp\"><code>@​matthewp</code></a>! - Adds the <code>astro preview --background</code> flag to start preview servers as background processes.</p>\n<p>This makes preview servers easier to manage from scripts and AI coding agents because the command returns after the server is ready instead of keeping the terminal attached to the long-running process.</p>\n<pre lang=\"sh\"><code>astro preview --background\n</code></pre>\n<p>When a preview server is running in the background, you can inspect or stop it with new <code>astro preview</code> subcommands:</p>\n<pre lang=\"sh\"><code>astro preview status\nastro preview logs\nastro preview logs --follow\nastro preview stop\n</code></pre>\n<p>If Astro detects that <code>astro preview</code> is being run by an AI coding agent, background mode is enabled automatically. This matches the existing behavior for <code>astro dev</code>, allowing agents to continue working after the preview server starts while still receiving the server URL and process ID.</p>\n<p>To opt out of automatic background mode for preview servers, set <code>ASTRO_PREVIEW_BACKGROUND=0</code> before running <code>astro preview</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/withastro/astro/pull/17532\">#17532</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/7f94895f8c28fc4d6977c9bfb1f90e80a9cfaa08\"><code>7f94895</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/florian-lefebvre\"><code>@​florian-lefebvre</code></a>! - Adds support for paths relative to your project root in <code>logger.entrypoint</code></p>\n<p>Previously, pointing <code>logger.entrypoint</code> at a custom log handler living in your own project required building an absolute <code>URL</code>. You can now write the path directly:</p>\n<pre lang=\"diff\"><code>// astro.config.mjs\nimport { defineConfig } from 'astro/config';\n<p>export default defineConfig({\nlogger: {</p>\n<ul>\n<li>entrypoint: new URL('./src/logger.js', import.meta.url),</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>entrypoint: './src/logger.js',\n},\n});\n</code></pre></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Paths starting with <code>./</code> or <code>../</code> are resolved against your project root. Package specifiers such as <code>@org/astro-logger</code>, absolute paths, and <code>URL</code> entrypoints keep working as before.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/withastro/astro/pull/17084\">#17084</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/961bbe5fdf4a761adb479595dfb94dc2e80f2957\"><code>961bbe5</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/matthewp\"><code>@​matthewp</code></a>! - Widens the <code>AstroPrerenderer</code> <code>render()</code> return type so prerenderers can report incremental-build metadata</p>\n<p>A prerenderer's <code>render()</code> may now resolve to either a <code>Response</code> (as before) or a <code>PrerenderResult</code> object that pairs the response with the content entries and optimized-image transforms the page resolved. This lets prerenderers that render out of process (for example, in an adapter's runtime like workerd) report those dependencies back to the build, so <a href=\"https://docs.astro.build/en/reference/experimental-flags/incremental-build/\">incremental static builds</a> can track and replay them for skipped pages.</p>\n<pre lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { AstroPrerenderer, PrerenderResult } from 'astro';\n<p></code></pre></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/60e94329f94438c1fc9b513bd9669bf07c89b680\"><code>60e9432</code></a> [ci] release (<a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/tree/HEAD/packages/astro/issues/17558\">#17558</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/af92694f05b6891eb2d13db149cde732ef9c9366\"><code>af92694</code></a> docs: slightly reword session options description (<a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/tree/HEAD/packages/astro/issues/17607\">#17607</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/caace2ec6e93139e18833e31f02f229ec2c90dc6\"><code>caace2e</code></a> [ci] format</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/0224a3a356c1f2956075b77c3667bc67cf027d8c\"><code>0224a3a</code></a> Add background mode for astro preview (<a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/tree/HEAD/packages/astro/issues/17174\">#17174</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/961bbe5fdf4a761adb479595dfb94dc2e80f2957\"><code>961bbe5</code></a> Experimental incremental static builds (<a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/tree/HEAD/packages/astro/issues/17084\">#17084</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/7f94895f8c28fc4d6977c9bfb1f90e80a9cfaa08\"><code>7f94895</code></a> feat(logger): allow passing relative string entrypoints (<a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/tree/HEAD/packages/astro/issues/17532\">#17532</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/90c98ae21ef0444a4088b7081676b0f97915001f\"><code>90c98ae</code></a> feat(session): add <code>session: false</code> to opt out of session support (<a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/tree/HEAD/packages/astro/issues/16871\">#16871</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/3ea55ce24024af7dc6ec3dcdde2f8af6ab5707d8\"><code>3ea55ce</code></a> Support detect devEngines for installs (<a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/tree/HEAD/packages/astro/issues/17579\">#17579</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/0089f836320ec2aefdb6c448af31e56754115c5c\"><code>0089f83</code></a> Fix Content Layer build crash when neotraverse 0.6.x is hoisted by another de...</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commit/f4150daf36f488987f6f07cbd20d59bebdb4b725\"><code>f4150da</code></a> [ci] format</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/commits/astro@7.2.0/packages/astro\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `shiki` from 4.3.1 to 4.4.2\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/shikijs/shiki/releases\">shiki's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v4.4.2</h2>\n<h3>   🐞 Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Unbreak CI after vite 8 bump and grammar/deps updates  -  by <a href=\"https://github.com/antfubot\"><code>@​antfubot</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/shikijs/shiki/issues/1300\">shikijs/shiki#1300</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/shikijs/shiki/commit/c5d310bb\"><!-- raw HTML omitted -->(c5d31)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>   🏎 Performance</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>core</strong>: Token split performance improvements  -  by <a href=\"https://github.com/amadeus\"><code>@​amadeus</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/shikijs/shiki/issues/1301\">shikijs/shiki#1301</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/shikijs/shiki/commit/41896281\"><!-- raw HTML omitted -->(41896)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h5>    <a href=\"https://github.com/shikijs/shiki/compare/v4.4.1...v4.4.2\">View changes on GitHub</a></h5>\n<h2>v4.4.1</h2>\n<h3>   🚀 Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Update deps  -  by <a href=\"https://github.com/antfu\"><code>@​antfu</code></a> <a href=\"https://github.com/shikijs/shiki/commit/e07fd5cc\"><!-- raw HTML omitted -->(e07fd)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h5>    <a href=\"https://github.com/shikijs/shiki/compare/v4.4.0...v4.4.1\">View changes on GitHub</a></h5>\n<h2>v4.4.0</h2>\n<h3>   🚀 Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Update grammars and themes  -  by <a href=\"https://github.com/antfu\"><code>@​antfu</code></a> <a href=\"https://github.com/shikijs/shiki/commit/dec2a327\"><!-- raw HTML omitted -->(dec2a)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>   🐞 Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>core</strong>: Guess yaml from frontmatter segments  -  by <a href=\"https://github.com/antfubot\"><code>@​antfubot</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/shikijs/shiki/issues/1299\">shikijs/shiki#1299</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/shikijs/shiki/commit/1b8b6e42\"><!-- raw HTML omitted -->(1b8b6)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h5>    <a href=\"https://github.com/shikijs/shiki/compare/v4.3.1...v4.4.0\">View changes on GitHub</a></h5>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/shikijs/shiki/commit/2aec8566cf186a92f4e094e6a92c335de3181ecd\"><code>2aec856</code></a> chore: release v4.4.2</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/shikijs/shiki/commit/c5d310bb07ef862a03751063091270a89369740c\"><code>c5d310b</code></a> fix: unbreak CI after vite 8 bump and grammar/deps updates (<a href=\"https://github.com/shikijs/shiki/tree/HEAD/packages/shiki/issues/1300\">#1300</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/shikijs/shiki/commit/407dca0cf9efdf66a8bfb2949679f9f2e41b1486\"><code>407dca0</code></a> chore: release v4.4.1</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/shikijs/shiki/commit/a64bab15e5cf0e1e494241d3dc3367e31acbbb10\"><code>a64bab1</code></a> chore: release v4.4.0</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/shikijs/shiki/commit/dec2a3273de8e225ff64d91874a1c53fde0ee75b\"><code>dec2a32</code></a> feat: update grammars and themes</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/shikijs/shiki/commits/v4.4.2/packages/shiki\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `web-vitals` from 5.3.0 to 6.1.0\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">web-vitals's changelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h3>v6.1.0 (2026-08-05)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add Resource Timing buffer for LCP attribution\n(<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/pull/776\">#776</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>v6.0.1 (2026-07-27)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Prevent JavaScript error if <code>PerformanceObserver</code> not available\n(<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/pull/772\">#772</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>v6.0.0 (2026-07-21)</h3>\n<p>v6 introduces <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/web-platform/soft-navigations\">Soft Navigation support for the Web Vitals metrics</a> when supported by the browser.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>[!NOTE]\nSee the <a href=\"https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/blob/main/docs/upgrading-to-v6.md\">upgrading to v6</a> guide for a complete list of all API changes in version 6.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>[BREAKING]</strong> Remove unneeded modules with tsconfig <code>verbatimModuleSyntax</code>\n(<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/pull/741\">#741</a>)</li>\n<li>Add source maps\n(<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/pull/771\">#771</a>)</li>\n<li>Cap RequestIdleCallback to 1 second to ensure metrics report even when busy\n(<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/pull/755\">#755</a>)</li>\n<li>Flip default for <code>includeProcessedEventEntries</code> to false for v6\n(<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/pull/763\">#763</a>)</li>\n<li>Add Soft Navigation support\n(<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/pull/308\">#308</a>)</li>\n<li>Add bfcache support for reporting small INP interactions\n(part of <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/pull/308\">#308</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/commit/85ca9dbd794eedb59eef1902c4b18ded70f6d6d5\"><code>85ca9db</code></a> Release v6.1.0</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/commit/eb6590a9069c6025e15ff311354642fe93ea9821\"><code>eb6590a</code></a> Prep CHANGELOG for v6.1.0</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/commit/3c850823f7f25f59fc9e02d873137c542d99fd42\"><code>3c85082</code></a> Add resource timing buffer for LCP (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/issues/776\">#776</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/commit/45a09da8f71986c81a971a4b1c84e9538acf027b\"><code>45a09da</code></a> Release v6.0.1</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/commit/e63150758a2dff7ac55e1d2a478a1c08858357d8\"><code>e631507</code></a> Update CHANGELOG for 6.0.1</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/commit/2d7ca2d701a47a62fa8ff9fe0fe7f4d627fdb8fa\"><code>2d7ca2d</code></a> Prevent JavaScript error if PerformanceObserver not available (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/issues/772\">#772</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/commit/d8895182c152d9f619549f04299e52cd80d246f0\"><code>d889518</code></a> Update README</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/commit/949d522766f9fa66722146bb162ece37ee429e73\"><code>949d522</code></a> Fix CHANGELOG</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/commit/67a9ddb4cf77f8d1cb2c877ccd870b9c821aa853\"><code>67a9ddb</code></a> Release v6.0.0</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/commit/11b0b222818d74cc14812b1657aa86fd32f26a12\"><code>11b0b22</code></a> Prep CHANGELOG and unique id prefix for v6.0.0 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/issues/764\">#764</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/compare/v5.3.0...v6.1.0\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />",
